------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HACKING_COMMON_DOC — adding a WCH family or subfamily
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Reconstructed from libopencm3's HACKING_COMMON_DOC and adapted for
libopenwch.  Follow the steps in order; the build fails loudly if one of the
mechanical steps is missed.

A. Root Makefile
----------------

1. Add the new library directory name to TARGETS.  This one variable drives
   recursive building, the IRQ header generation, the style check paths and
   `make list-targets`.

2. Add an IRQ_FILES_<target> variable for it (see the block above the
   $(IRQ_GENERATED_FILES) rule) and to IRQ_GENERATED_FILES.

B. include/
-----------

3. Create include/libopenwch/<family>/.

4. Add include/libopenwch/<family>/irq.json.  `index` is the *vector table
   slot*, which is also the PFIC interrupt id.  Slots 0..15 are reserved for
   RISC-V exceptions, so external interrupts start at 16.  Slots without an
   entry are filled with reserved handlers automatically.

5. Add include/libopenwch/<family>/memorymap.h with every peripheral base
   address and the bus bases.  Include
   <libopenwch/qingke/memorymap.h> for the core region.

6. The family's Doxygen groups are declared centrally in
   doc/source/groups.dox, guarded by @if <family> ... @endif.  Add
   @defgroup <FAMILY>, @defgroup <FAMILY>_defines, and the family overview
   text there.  (The libopencm3 per-family doc-<family>.h style is not used,
   so one file cannot be left out when a family is added.)

7. Add the per-peripheral device headers
   include/libopenwch/<family>/<periph>.h.  Each one:

     * has the family-scoped Doxygen block,
     * guards with LIBOPENWCH_<PERIPH>_H (the SAME guard as other families,
       so only one family can be active in a translation unit),
     * includes <libopenwch/<family>/common/<periph>_common_<v1>.h>,
     * adds the family-specific defines,
     * declares the prototypes inside BEGIN_DECLS/END_DECLS.

8. Add the shared implementation headers
   include/libopenwch/<family>/common/<periph>_common_<variant>.h.  They must
   not be included directly; use the libopencm3 double-guard pattern:

	/* THIS FILE SHOULD NOT BE INCLUDED DIRECTLY, BUT ONLY VIA GPIO.H */
	/** @cond */
	#if defined(LIBOPENWCH_GPIO_H)
	/** @endcond */
	#ifndef LIBOPENWCH_GPIO_COMMON_V1_H
	#define LIBOPENWCH_GPIO_COMMON_V1_H
	...
	#endif
	/** @cond */
	#else
	#warning "... should not be included explicitly, only via gpio.h"
	#endif
	/** @endcond */

9. Extend include/libopenwch/dispatch/nvic.h with a branch that selects the
   new family's generated nvic.h from its -D<FAMILY> define.  The define must
   equal the TARGETS entry (upper-cased) because both genlink-config.mk and
   the family Makefile set it.

C. lib/
-------

10. Create lib/<family>/ with a Makefile that sets:

	LIBNAME         libopenwch_<family>
	SRCLIBDIR       $(OPENWCH_TOP)/lib     (absolute; see the note there)
	OPENWCH_TOP     $(abspath $(CURDIR)/../..)
	VPATH           .:$(OPENWCH_QINGKE):$(OPENWCH_COMMON)
	TGT_CFLAGS      -I$(OPENWCH_INC) -march=... -mabi=... -D<FAMILY>
	OBJS            vector_handlers.o vector_names.o plus the drivers
	ARFLAGS         rcs

    and ends with `include $(OPENWCH_TOP)/lib/Makefile.include`.
    Use $(abspath), not relative '../..': relative paths are unreliable under
    virtualised filesystems.

11. Add lib/<family>/common/<periph>_common_<variant>.c implementations.  Each
    must #include the *device* header (e.g. <libopenwch/ch32v0/gpio.h>) so that
    the family's register names are visible.

12. If the core needs family-specific configuration, provide
    lib/<family>/common/vector_chipset.c overriding the weak
    openwch_chipset_core_configure() / openwch_chipset_early_init().

D. Linker and device database
-----------------------------

13. Add the part-number lines and the group's `+` / `END` lines to
    ld/devices.data.  Read ld/README first: the two pattern rules there are
    what make the traversal terminate.

14. Add a ld/tests/<part>.data marker and a matching <part>.result file, then
    run `make genlinktests`.

E. Documentation
----------------

15. Add the family to the TARGETS default in doc/Makefile.

16. Add the family's @if block to doc/source/groups.dox and, if it appears in
    the main page table or prose, to doc/source/mainpage.dox.  A family that
    has optional extra sources (currently only ch5xx58x, which adds the BLE
    layer) must also extend the per-family extra-input selection in
    doc/Makefile.

17. Run `make html`, check that doc/<family>/doxygen.log is empty, and open
    doc/<family>/html/index.html.  The build skips cleanly if Doxygen is not
    installed, so add an explicit note in the commit/status when it was not
    actually exercised.

F. Housekeeping
---------------

18. Add the LGPL header to every new file.
19. Update README.md's supported-part list.
20. Run `make stylecheck` and, if the family introduced new documented
    symbols, confirm that the @defgroup names do not collide with another
    family's.
